From 8ad4bbe6aa14a4e305da23f2f24b57a5c180145e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tstoltz <tristan.stoltz@evolvingresonantcocreationism.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 00:45:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add native grouped-signature policy primitive (Model N)

Second slice of the admission-boundary experiment for nix-signature-policy
(see /srv/luminous-dynamics/nix-signature-policy) -- the native
grouped-signature baseline ("Model N" in the empirical comparison: Nix
verifies signatures and directly enforces groups/thresholds itself, no
external hook or IPC).

allSignatureGroupsSatisfied(verified, groups): a KeyGroup names a set of
key identities that must ALL appear among already-verified signature
observations for the group to be satisfied; the whole policy requires
every configured group satisfied. Deliberately a pure function over
ValidPathInfo::VerifiedSignature observations (from
checkSignaturesDetailed(), landed in the prior commit on this branch),
never raw signature bytes or a public-key registry -- mirrors
nix-signature-policy's own core-v1 separation of representation-neutral
policy from cryptographic verification, and makes this trivially
unit-testable with hand-built observations, no real keys needed.

Not wired into any admission path yet (pathInfoIsUntrusted/addToStore) --
this commit is the policy primitive and its test coverage only, matching
this branch's established staging discipline of no-behavior-change
commits with an explicit next step. Test coverage includes the exact
benchmark policy this comparison is built around: built-in trust AND
both an Ed25519 and ML-DSA-65 signature from one configured publisher,
expressed as two distinct per-algorithm key names in one group -- never
one name trusted under both algorithms, per this project's own verified
same-name-collision finding.

Built and tested in an isolated working-tree copy after discovering a
second, concurrently active session already iterating on this same
branch's hook-invocation machinery (authorization-caller.{cc,hh},
local-store.cc wiring) in the original checkout -- this commit
deliberately touches none of those files.
